# CODEOWNERS for ssh-perma-tunnel.
#
# `@<owner>` is a placeholder — replace with the GitHub handle (or team
# slug, e.g. `@my-org/spt-maintainers`) that should receive review
# requests. Until that substitution happens, GitHub will silently treat
# unresolved handles as no-owner; merging will not be blocked, but
# review-required protections won't fire.
#
# Order matters: later patterns win for the same path.

# Default fallback owner — every file in the repo.
*                       @<owner>

# Sensitive areas — require explicit maintainer review.
/crates/spt-snmp/       @<owner>
/packaging/             @<owner>
/.github/               @<owner>
SECURITY.md             @<owner>
